# Git Workshop Project

**Name:** Jezreel Ruiz

**Project Title:** GIT TUTORIAL

**Brief Description:**
This is a simple HTML web page I've done. The project was made to practice using Git for tracking changes and maintaining the history of the project.

**Reflection:**
The difference between `git add` and `git commit` is that `git add` prepares and stages the changes that I want to include, while `git commit` saves those staged changes as a new version in the Git history. In simple terms, `git add` selects the changes, while `git commit` records them.
